# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# Two warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 27 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, each with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with `{}'." Fires on literal
#       set, tuple and sign notation carrying a sub- or superscript ---
#       $\{0,1\}^{\ell}$, $(-1)^{\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle}$,
#       $(1-2p)^{r}$, $(\pi \circ H + H)_{\pi}$ --- where the script attaches
#       to the closing delimiter exactly as intended.  (2 hits)
#   8   "Wrong length of dash may have been used." Two hits, both inside a
#       sentence quoted verbatim from the source, where the source's own text
#       sets off an aside with en-dashes. Changing them would misquote.  (2 hits)
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each hit is the final
#       character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the source paper. The
#       punctuation belongs to the quoted text; moving it out would misquote.  (3 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 27 August 2026 the file is clean under this
# config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n8
    -n38
}
